     1	"""Run A (docs/revision/followup2/runner-up-plan.md): the full-budget runner-up comparator C-thr(K=12) on the six fresh
     2	markets at rho 0.2, under D2+H3 and X7-SC, with the frozen stage functions of scripts/revision_v2.py.
     3	
     4	The frozen code identifies a rule by its label and reads its parameters from `params["cred"]`. The runner-up therefore
     5	runs under the label "C*" with the runner-up's credibility parameters, in its own output directory; its records differ
     6	from the registered C* records by `rule_params_sha256`, and `label.json` names the rule. The driver refuses an output
     7	that contains a copy of a registered C* record. Its reference is selected by the frozen reference stage from the
     8	registered C* menu construction: its own D2+H3 and X7-SC searches plus the cuts-3 bank of the other rules' registered
     9	winners (the registered C* winner is excluded, as C* excluded itself).
    10	
    11	Order: bank inputs (hash-checked against the original freeze), preflight, searches (D2+H3, then X7-SC), references,
    12	the follow-up freeze, acceptance, evaluation, acceptance, doubling, analysis, inventory. Exploratory; no registered
    13	estimate or decision changes."""
