    93	categories are applied to the nominal pooled interval with the margin 0.05, labelled exploratory. The intervals are
    94	conditional on these six markets and the selected policies and references; they exclude search and market-sampling
    95	uncertainty and carry no registered calibration or Holm guarantee. The doubling check's attack and reference changes
    96	and its flag are reported per cell.
    97	
    98	## 4. Expectation (written before any runner-up result)
    99	
   100	E: pooled g(C*) - g(C-thr12) > 0 under D2+H3, computed exactly from the paired per-seed values (not against a rounded
   101	threshold). Met if it holds under both base and doubled records; failed if it fails under both (a tie, exactly 0, is not
   102	met); not established if they disagree; "not available" if a record is missing or a value is nonfinite (reported
   103	separately, never a failure). No expectation on the category.
   104	
   105	## 5. Cost and spending controls
   106	
   107	`python3 docs/revision/followup2/cost_estimate.py`: 17.65 core-hours, 1.91 USD at the benchmark's 0.108 USD per
   108	core-hour; billed path on one 16-vCPU pod 3.56 hours (reproduction gate 0.61 h, searches, six serial reference calls,
   109	X7-SC evaluation and doubling, 0.3 h preparation and tail) = 1.99 USD at 0.56 USD per hour. Estimate 1.99 USD
   110	(x 1.25 = 2.49); **stop cap and reservation 3.00 USD**, the full allowance, in the ledger category `followup` (cap 22 USD
   111	shared by all follow-up runs: reset 5, churn 8, Run A 3, Run B 4.25, total 20.25; `budget_followup.py reserve`). A paid run
   112	requires `--started-at <allocation time>` and the launcher's attempts file (`--attempts`). The driver checks
   113	the cap between stages: a stage starts only if the billed time so far
   114	plus its estimate stays within the cap; a running stage is never killed (author's instruction); the run stops, writes
   115	`cost_stop.json` and an inventory, and reports. This is an admission limit, not a billing ceiling: a stage that starts
   116	within the cap finishes, and the pod is deleted after it.
   117	
   118	**Launcher handoff (draft 5).** The launcher copy pushes to the pod, before every paid driver call, its current
   119	`<name>.attempts` file and the ledger, and passes `--attempts`, `--ledger`, `--run-tag`, `--started-at` (the current pod's
   120	allocation time), `--usd-per-hour` (the price ceiling MAXCPH), `--stop-file /root/STOP`, and `--soft-deadline` (its soft
   121	deadline). The driver reads the launcher's own event lines (`<pod> <epoch> start`, `<pod> <epoch> deleted`;
   122	`guards.attempts_spend`): each closed attempt counts at the ceiling, the open start is the current pod (counted from
   123	`--started-at`), and malformed or unordered lines are refused (tests with lines in the launcher's exact format); spend of
   124	earlier launches comes from the ledger rows tagged with the run tag, since the launcher truncates its file per launch. The
   125	driver checks the STOP file and the soft deadline before each internal stage or round, so a single `--stage all` call
   126	honours the launcher's between-stage stop (test).
   127	
   128	**Launcher and the cap.** The pod launcher is a copy of `results/pods/reset_pod.sh` with `results/pods/podctl.py`. Its soft
   129	deadline is the cap at the price ceiling MAXCPH, counted from the first creation request of the launch, so it holds across
   130	attempts; at the soft deadline the remote script stops before its next stage (a STOP file read between stages), and the
   131	driver's own admission check (`--cap-usd`, `--started-at`, `--attempts`) stops between stages or rounds as well. A running
   132	stage is never stopped (the author: do not kill jobs). The single exception is the watchdog, which deletes the pod at 1.3 x
   133	the cap at the price ceiling; that is the only mid-stage stop. Closed attempts are listed in the launcher's
   134	`<name>.attempts` file (pod, start, end, price), which the driver reads (`guards.prior_from_attempts`) and counts toward the
   135	cap before each paid attempt; a paid run without it is refused (no default of zero); after the launch the spend is recorded
   136	in the ledger (`budget_v2.py --record`).
   137	
   138	## 6. Steps
   139	
   140	1. Internal review to consensus; freeze this plan.
   141	2. Reserve 3.00 USD in the ledger; one pod: `reset_followup_v2.py --reproduce --require-identical`, then `runnerup_v2.py
   142	   --stage all --workers 12 --reset-mac M --reset-pod P --doubling-evidence D --cap-usd 3.00 --started-at T --attempts A --ledger L --run-tag runner-up --stop-file /root/STOP --soft-deadline S`; delete and verify the pod; record the spend.
   143	3. Analysis on the Mac from the retrieved records; a paper paragraph and table labelled exploratory, after review.
